        <item rdf:about="https://www.mdpi.com/2078-2489/17/10/1033">

	<title>Information, Vol. 17, Pages 1033: Multi-Level Transformations Induced by GenAI in Instructional Design: A Thematic Analysis of a Reddit Forum</title>
	<link>https://www.mdpi.com/2078-2489/17/10/1033</link>
	<description>Research on generative artificial intelligence (GenAI) integration into instructional design practice has been expanding rapidly; however, its effects on the instructional design profession remain underexplored. To this end, this study examines instructional designers&amp;amp;rsquo; perceptions about how GenAI is reshaping the instructional design professional landscape and how online communities engage them in sharing those perceptions. Using a mixed-methods data analysis method including automatic text mining and human verification, a large data set obtained from an online community of instructional designers on Reddit was analyzed thematically. Results revealed three key changes at professional, organizational, and individual levels, and the mechanisms shaping instructional designers&amp;amp;rsquo; engagement in their online community. Namely, GenAI has already started to reshape the instructional design landscape through a mixed set of changes including transformations, adaptations and reconfigurations, and an online community can function as an informal community of practice for instructional designers to collectively share experiential wisdom and necessary competencies to successfully navigate the emergent transitions. This study contributes by uncovering the changes happening in instructional design due to GenAI and how informal online channels can work as communities of practice that are distributed, asynchronous, on-demand knowledge exchange avenues, thus increasing instructional designers&amp;amp;rsquo; awareness and collective preparedness.</description>
	<pubDate>2026-10-17</pubDate>

	<content:encoded><![CDATA[
	<p><b>Information, Vol. 17, Pages 1033: Multi-Level Transformations Induced by GenAI in Instructional Design: A Thematic Analysis of a Reddit Forum</b></p>
